      "text": "To find the length of \\( QS \\), we start by analyzing the given information in the problem. We know that \\( \\cos R = \\frac{4}{9} \\) and that \\( \\triangle SQR \\) is a right triangle with \\( \\angle SQR = 90^\\circ \\).\n\nGiven that \\( \\cos R = \\frac{4}{9} \\), we can use the definition of cosine in a right triangle, which is the ratio of the adjacent side to the hypotenuse. Here, the adjacent side to \\( \\angle R \\) is \\( QR \\) and the hypotenuse is \\( SQ \\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\cos R = \\frac{QR}{SQ} = \\frac{4}{9}\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\( QR = 9 \\). Let \\( SQ = x \\). Then, we can write:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{9}{x} = \\frac{4}{9}\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we solve the equation by cross-multiplying:\n\n\\[\n9 \\cdot 9 = 4 \\cdot x \\implies 81 = 4x \\implies x = \\frac{81}{4}\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of \\( SQ \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{81}{4}}\n\\]",
